From beb636deaf8422dd74e74193df59521b6b02926c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 06:01:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2284/2312] media: uapi: add AVS2 stateless decoder pixel
 format and controls

Add the V4L2_PIX_FMT_AVS2_FRAME pixel format and four stateless codec
controls for AVS2 (GB/T 33475.2, IEEE 1857.4) decoding:

- V4L2_CID_STATELESS_AVS2_SEQUENCE: sequence header syntax elements;
- V4L2_CID_STATELESS_AVS2_PICTURE: picture header syntax elements and
  the reference picture list, resolved by the application from the
  reference configuration set. Each reference carries its own reference
  picture order counts, which the hardware needs for the temporal motion
  vector prediction from the co-located picture;
- V4L2_CID_STATELESS_AVS2_WEIGHT_QUANT: the weighting quantization
  matrices which apply to the picture;
- V4L2_CID_STATELESS_AVS2_ALF: the adaptive loop filter parameters.

An output buffer holds one coded picture, from its picture header (which
sequence headers may precede) to the end of its last slice, as found in
the elementary stream. Hardware which parses the slices itself is given
the offset of the first slice.

The controls take the CID range at the stateless codec base + 900 and
the control types 0x02c0 to 0x02c3.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
